# C5 result at f8e45c378c8d40aaed537317dc793f91053c1886

Implementation: "'`ConcreteSpec/Spec/Own.lean`, `ConcreteSpec/Spec/Grant.lean`.
Proofs: `ConcreteSpec/Proofs/Own.lean`, `ConcreteSpec/Proofs/Grant.lean`.
All four modules are imported into the library. Existing fragments and protected upstream
modules are unchanged. Nothing was pushed and no history was rewritten.

## Theorem catalog

Names below are relative to `ConcreteSpec.Core` and the indicated namespace. These summarize
the Lean statements for review; the Lean statements remain the specification.

### Own

| Theorem | Statement |
|---|---|
| `validate_iff` | Success returns exactly the candidate, and that candidate is well formed. |
| `validate_wf` | A successfully validated result is well formed. |
| `move_preserves` | Successful owner move leaves a well-formed state. |
| `reinitialize_preserves` | Successful reinitialization leaves a well-formed state. |
| `borrow_preserves` | Successful owner borrowing leaves a well-formed state. |
| `reborrowAt_preserves` | Successful reborrowing into a specified activation leaves a well-formed state. |
| `reborrow_preserves` | Successful reborrowing in the current activation leaves a well-formed state. |
| `endLoan_preserves` | Successfully ending a childless loan leaves a well-formed state. |
| `accessOwner_preserves` | Successful shared/mutable owner access leaves a well-formed state. |
| `accessLoan_preserves` | Successful shared/mutable loan access leaves a well-formed state. |
| `bind_preserves` | Successful fresh binding or reinitialization leaves a well-formed state. |
| `drop_preserves` | Successful local-scope removal leaves a well-formed state. |
| `enter_preserves` | Successful activation entry with owning parameters leaves a well-formed state. |
| `endLocals_preserves` | Ending an activation'"'s loans preserves an initially well-formed state. |
| "'`leave_preserves` | Successful activation exit leaves a well-formed state. |
| `enterDown_preserves` | The standalone downward-lending call-boundary transition leaves a well-formed state. |
| `life_preserves` | Every successful owner lifecycle event leaves a well-formed state. |
| `loan_has_owned_root` | Every active loan has a slot holding its original root in owned status. |
| `moved_no_loan` | A moved slot cannot be the root of an active loan. |
| `instrument_erasure` | A successful permission/concrete-operation composition has exactly the uninstrumented concrete result and store. |
| `life_erasure` | Successful lifecycle instrumentation leaves the concrete store unchanged. |
| `adoptDown_preserves` | Adopting pending argument loans into a callee leaves a well-formed state. |
| `passDown_preserves` | Opening and marking a downward argument loan leaves ownership well formed. |
| `callLife_preserves` | The C1 callback for mixed owning/view parameters leaves ownership well formed. |
| `callLife_erasure` | That callback leaves the arbitrary concrete store unchanged. |
| `instrument_preserves` | Instrumenting a concrete operation with any invariant-preserving permission transition preserves ownership. |
| `readOwner_erasure` | Successful owner read returns exactly the C4 value and leaves concrete storage unchanged. |
| `writeOwner_erasure` | Successful owner write has exactly the C4 write effect. |
| `readLoan_erasure` | Successful scalar loan read resolves its active whole-root loan and returns exactly C4'"'s value without changing storage. |
| "'`writeLoan_erasure` | Successful scalar loan write resolves its active whole-root loan and has exactly C4'"'s write effect. |
| "'`nextLoan_fresh` | The next loan identity differs from every active loan'"'s identity. |
| "'`borrow_birth` | Owner borrowing issues the old counter, increments it once, and retains the requested root/path. |
| `reborrow_birth` | Reborrowing issues the old counter, increments it once, keeps the original root, extends the projection, and records its parent. |
| `endLoan_supply` | Ending a loan does not decrement or otherwise change the identity supply. |
| `leave_no_local_loan` | No loan after successful call exit is rooted in any of the callee'"'s named locals. |
| "'`adoptDown_only_arguments` | Every adopted identity was marked as a pending argument in the input state. |
| `leave_no_activation_slot` | Successful exit leaves no slot belonging to the departing activation, even with an incomplete locals table. |

Private helpers: `fold_preserves` lifts invariant preservation through a successful list fold;
`slot_unique` derives slot equality from equal keys in a unique-key list; `endLoan_frames`
shows loan ending leaves activation frames unchanged; `fold_frames` lifts that equality through
a fold; `drop_absent` proves selected local roots are absent after successful scope removal.

### Generative

| Theorem | Statement |
|---|---|
| `validate_iff` | Success returns exactly the candidate, which is well formed. |
| `fresh_preserves` | A fresh generative binder leaves a well-formed state. |
| `depend_preserves` | Successful dependency registration leaves a well-formed state. |
| `consume_preserves` | Successful explicit dependency consumption leaves a well-formed state. |
| `release_preserves` | Successful allocator release leaves a well-formed state. |
| `reset_preserves` | Successful allocator reset leaves a well-formed state. |
| `endScope_preserves` | Successful lexical scope exit leaves a well-formed state. |
| `nextBrand_fresh` | The next nominal brand differs from every currently scoped brand. |
| `fresh_generation` | A new binder issues the old brand counter and increments it once. |
| `reset_generation` | Every reset issues the old brand counter and increments it once. |
| `endScope_non_escape` | No remaining dependent mentions a brand bound in a successfully ended scope, including phantom occurrences. |
| `allocations_have_live_allocator` | Every allocation dependency has a still-live allocator witness of the same nominal brand. |
| `instrument_erasure` | Successful brand instrumentation has exactly the concrete allocator operation'"'s result and state. |

### Grants

| Theorem | Statement |
|---|---|
| "'`usable_some` | Successful resource use is lookup of the same resource with its live flag true. |
| `consumed_bounded` | Marking a resource consumed preserves the initial rights bound. |
| `consumed_fresh` | Marking a resource consumed preserves the identity-supply bound. |
| `issue_bounded` | Issuing a resource whose rights are within budget preserves that budget for the whole state. |
| `issue_fresh` | Fresh issuance preserves the supply bound and advances the supply. |
| `narrow_bounded` | Successful narrowing preserves the launch rights budget. |
| `acquire_bounded` | Successful checked acquisition preserves the launch rights budget. |
| `close_bounded` | Successful close on either result preserves the rights budget. |
| `rights_never_grow` | Any finite sequence of narrowing, acquisition and close stays within the initial rights budget. |
| `narrow_fresh` | Narrowing preserves the supply bound. |
| `acquire_fresh` | Acquisition preserves the supply bound. |
| `close_fresh` | Close preserves the supply bound. |
| `dead_unusable` | A historically consumed resource identity cannot be used. |
| `consumed_dead` | Consumption of a present resource records its identity as dead. |
| `consumed_keeps_dead` | Consumption cannot revive any already-dead identity. |
| `issue_keeps_dead` | Fresh issuance cannot revive any already-dead identity. |
| `close_consumes` | Every specified close result, success or Copy error, consumes its input. |
| `narrow_consumes` | Narrowing consumes its input even though it creates a descendant. |
| `consumed_never_revives` | Any finite allowed operation sequence preserves dead identities and the supply bound. |
| `narrow_intersection` | Narrowing retains the same opaque handle and returns precisely parent rights intersected with requested rights. |
| `acquire_keeps_parent` | Acquisition leaves its parent'"'s resource, rights and usability exactly unchanged. |

Private helper: "'`update_all` preserves a per-entry predicate under an association-list update
whose value transformation preserves that predicate.

## Scope and limitations

The executable ownership/brand reference semantics checks a finite invariant on a candidate;
it never repairs the candidate. The preservation theorems establish successful transitions,
not checker/elaborator correspondence or completeness of admission.

`Hybrid.Place` is reused, with descriptors for scalar payload representation and separately
supplied checked Copy/mutability facts. C9 must relate these facts to its richer semantic type
identities. No third place identity is introduced. Logical field/index paths are retained and
whole-root conflicts apply to every path. Concrete nonempty-projection resolution waits for
aggregate layout; whole scalar reads/writes are connected to C4 now.

The call adapter requires checked callee binder identities in argument metadata. Views stay in
instrumentation rather than ordinary stored/returned values. It opens the child while evaluating
the argument, before later argument accesses, then adopts only marked pending argument loans.

Brands implement nominal generation, reset generations, dependency lifetimes, and lexical
non-escape. Existential package syntax/elaboration and structural dependency extraction are
integration duties. Concrete heap release contexts, allocator algorithms, OS acquisition/close
adapters, the target/network grant tables, Entropy'"'s shape, and C6–C10 are outside this task.
Grant runtime handles remain opaque concrete values; no resource-state erasure is assumed.
Ownership transitions such as close do not replace the independent static authority judgment.

## Review and validation

Review round 1 found unrestricted adoption and activation slots omitted from locals tables.
Both were fixed with refused examples and explicit theorems. Round 2 is clean, recorded in
local git notes at the head above; REVIEW_PUSH=0 prevented all note pushes. The first review
piece reported sandbox startup prevented context reads, so its clean verdict is limited to the
provided diff. No additional non-Codex reviewer was available.

At the head above, scripts/spec/rules.sh passed (32 checks), including the library build.
The final trust-ban result is recorded in the final response. Heavy axiom inventory, kernel
replay, external checkers and the full gate set were not run locally, as instructed.

## QUESTIONS

None requiring an owner answer. No language decision is revised and no protected-module
change is needed. The deferred integrations above are not treated as approved new semantics.
